<header>
  <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &gt; <a href="/lesson37">JavaScript Course</a> &gt; Lesson 37 - Quiz App</p>
  <p><a id="homeLink" href="/">← Back to Home</a> | JavaScript Course - Lesson 37 / 50</p>
  <h1>Lesson 37: Quiz App - Questions, Timer & Score</h1>
  <p>Build a Real Quiz Like This Website | LearnHTMLCSSJS.com</p>
</header>

<div class="container">
  <div class="tabs">
    <button id="lessonTabBtn" class="tab-btn active" onclick="showLesson()">📖 Lesson</button>
    <button id="testTabBtn" class="tab-btn" onclick="showTest()">📝 Test - 100 Marks</button>
  </div>
  <div id="lockMsg" class="lock-msg">🔒 Test is running! All tabs are locked until you submit the test or time ends.</div>

  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. What Will We Build?</h2>
    <p>Today we build a <b>real Quiz App</b> - Just like the tests on this website. It shows one question at a time, 4 options, a timer, a progress bar, instant correct/wrong feedback, and a final result screen with score.</p>
    <p>This project uses: <b>Array of Objects</b> for questions, <b>Variables</b> for current question and score, <b>Functions</b> for show, check, next, <b>DOM</b> to update screen, <b>Timer</b> for countdown, <b>If-Else</b> to check answers.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>How It Works - 3 Variables Control Everything:</b> <code>current = 0</code> - Which question are we on? <code>score = 0</code> - How many correct? <code>questions = [...]</code> - All questions data. Show question[current], check answer, current++, show next. When current reaches end, show result.</div>
    <h2>2. LIVE DEMO - Try Your Quiz App</h2>
    <p>Play the full quiz - 5 questions, 60 seconds, instant feedback:</p>
    <div class="demo-card">
      <div class="quiz-wrap">
        <div id="demoStart" style="text-align:center">
          <h3 style="margin:0">🧠 HTML CSS JS Quiz</h3>
          <p style="color:#64748b">5 Questions | 60 Seconds | Instant Result</p>
          <button class="btn btn-js" onclick="startDemoQuiz()">Start Quiz ▶️</button>
        </div>
        <div id="demoQuiz" style="display:none">
          <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:13px;color:#64748b"><span id="demoQCount">Question 1 / 5</span><span>⏰ <b id="demoTimer">60</b> sec</span></div>
          <div class="quiz-progress"><div class="quiz-progress-bar" id="demoProgress"></div></div>
          <h3 id="demoQText" style="margin:8px 0">Question?</h3>
          <div id="demoOptions"></div>
          <p id="demoFeedback" style="font-weight:bold;min-height:22px"></p>
          <button class="btn btn-next" id="demoNextBtn" style="display:none;width:100%" onclick="demoNext()">Next Question →</button>
        </div>
        <div id="demoResult" style="display:none;text-align:center">
          <h3 id="demoResultText" style="margin:0">Result</h3>
          <p id="demoResultMsg" style="color:#64748b"></p>
          <button class="btn" onclick="startDemoQuiz()">Play Again ↺</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <h2>3. Step 1 - Data - Array of Question Objects</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let questions = [</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">question: "What does HTML stand for?",</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">options: ["Hyper Text Markup Language", "High Tech Modern Language", "Home Tool Markup Language", "Hyperlink Text Mode Language"],</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">answer: 0 // Correct option index - First option</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">},</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">question: "Which tag makes a heading?",</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">options: ["&lt;p&gt;", "&lt;h1&gt;", "&lt;div&gt;", "&lt;span&gt;"],</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">answer: 1</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="text">];</span>
    </code></div>
    <p>Each question is an object with 3 keys: <code>question</code> = Text, <code>options</code> = Array of 4 answers, <code>answer</code> = Index of correct option (0, 1, 2, or 3).</p>
    <h2>4. Step 2 - showQuestion() - Show One Question</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let current = 0; // Question number</span><br>
<span class="text">let score = 0; // Correct answers</span><br><br>
<span class="text">function showQuestion() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let q = questions[current];</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("qText").innerText = q.question;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let html = "";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">for (let i = 0; i < q.options.length; i++) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">html += `&lt;button onclick="checkAnswer(${i})"&gt;${q.options[i]}&lt;/button&gt;`;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("options").innerHTML = html;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("count").innerText = "Question " + (current + 1) + " / " + questions.length;</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>5. Step 3 - checkAnswer() - Correct or Wrong?</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">function checkAnswer(selected) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let q = questions[current];</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let buttons = document.querySelectorAll(".opt");</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (selected === q.answer) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">score++; // Correct - Add 1</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">buttons[selected].style.backgroundColor = "green";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("feedback").innerText = "✅ Correct!";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">} else {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">buttons[selected].style.backgroundColor = "red";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">buttons[q.answer].style.backgroundColor = "green"; // Show correct one</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("feedback").innerText = "❌ Wrong! Correct is: " + q.options[q.answer];</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Disable all buttons - User cannot change answer</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">buttons.forEach(b => b.disabled = true);</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("nextBtn").style.display = "block";</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>6. Step 4 - nextQuestion() + Timer + Result</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">function nextQuestion() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">current++; // Go to next question</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (current < questions.length) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">showQuestion(); // More questions left</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">} else {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">showResult(); // No more questions</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="text">function showResult() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("quiz").style.display = "none";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("result").style.display = "block";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("result").innerText = "Your Score: " + score + " / " + questions.length;</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Timer - 60 seconds for full quiz</span><br>
<span class="text">let timeLeft = 60;</span><br>
<span class="text">let timer = setInterval(function() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">timeLeft--;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("timer").innerText = timeLeft;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (timeLeft <= 0) { clearInterval(timer); showResult(); }</span><br>
<span class="text">}, 1000);</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>7. Complete Example - Mini Quiz in One File</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;body&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;h2</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"qText"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h2&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"options"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"nextQuestion()"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Next</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;script&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let questions = [</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">{ question: "2 + 2 = ?", options: ["3", "4", "5", "6"], answer: 1 },</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">{ question: "Capital of Pakistan?", options: ["Lahore", "Karachi", "Islamabad", "Peshawar"], answer: 2 }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">];</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let current = 0, score = 0;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">function showQuestion() { let q = questions[current]; document.getElementById("qText").innerText = q.question; let h = ""; for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) { h += "&lt;button onclick='checkAnswer(" + i + ")'&gt;" + q.options[i] + "&lt;/button&gt;&lt;br&gt;"; } document.getElementById("options").innerHTML = h; }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">function checkAnswer(s) { if (s === questions[current].answer) { score++; alert("Correct!"); } else { alert("Wrong!"); } }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">function nextQuestion() { current++; if (current < questions.length) showQuestion(); else alert("Done! Score: " + score + "/" + questions.length); }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">showQuestion();</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/script&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/body&gt;</span> <span class="tag">&lt;/html&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>8. Homework - Make It Better</h2>
    <p>In Playground, add these to your Quiz:</p>
    <p>1. 10 Questions on any topic - HTML, Math, GK - With 4 options each<br>2. Timer per question - 15 seconds per question, auto-next when time ends<br>3. High Score - Save best score in LocalStorage, show "Best Score: X" on start screen</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> Questions = Array of objects { question, options[4], answer: index } | current = Which question now | score = How many correct | showQuestion() = Show current question + options | checkAnswer(selected) = Compare selected === answer | Disable buttons after answer | nextQuestion() = current++ , if end show result | Timer = setInterval, at 0 show result | Progress = (current / total) * 100</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> <a href="/lesson38">Lesson 38 - Password Generator</a> - Build a tool that creates strong random passwords.</p>
